Package: mozc-character-pad
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: tegaki-zinnia-japanese
Description: standalone character palette and handwriting input tools from mozc
 character_palette and hand_writing are two GUI tools that used to be
 bundled with Google Japanese Input (mozc), removed from mozc upstream in
 2020. This package restores them as standalone tools that do not require
 the mozc conversion engine (mozc_server) to be installed: selecting a
 character copies it to the clipboard instead of sending it to mozc_server
 over IPC.
 .
  * character_palette: browse Unicode / Shift-JIS (CP932) / JIS X
    0201/0208/0212 character tables and pick a character.
  * hand_writing: recognize hand-drawn characters using the zinnia engine
    and pick a candidate. Requires a zinnia handwriting model, e.g. from
    the tegaki-zinnia-japanese package, at
    /usr/share/tegaki/models/zinnia/handwriting-ja.model.
